Chat backend (./chatbackend on the server, not in this repo): let a tapped push
open its chat, and let the app unregister a device on sign-out.

- A chat push's data now carries peerUuid and peerName (the sender), so the app
  can open that conversation when the notification is tapped.
- DELETE /chat/dm/device-token { token }: removes this device's push token for
  the signed-in user, so the next account on the phone doesn't get the
  previous one's message notifications.

Applied on the server 2026-10-31 (backup: ~/backups/chatbackend-src-20261031-pre-push.tgz).
Apply after chat-blocks.patch:
  cd ~/treepnet/chatbackend && patch -p1 < chat-push-open-and-unregister.patch
  cd .. && docker compose build chatbackend && docker compose up -d chatbackend

